<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Abdul Qawi Mackawee</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Abdul Qawi Mackawee was a nationalist politician in the British-ruled State of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aden">Aden</a>. Appointed chief minister in 1965, he sided with the nationalists against the Federation of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/south-arabia">South Arabia</a> and British policy and was dismissed later that year, after which <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a> ruled Aden directly. He later led the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/front-for-the-liberation-of-occupied-south-yemen">Front for the Liberation of Occupied South Yemen</a> (FLOSY).</p></div>
